From 830ceaadc1a6fea9d93ce2def07b212bf669bc3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GNU-slop-enjoyer <johnepstein420@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:42:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kd: draw the text console on a UEFI framebuffer

UEFI machines have no VGA text mode. When the boot loader passes an
RGB framebuffer (24 or 32 bpp) through multiboot2, kd's display hooks
keep its 80x25 cell grid in a shadow buffer and draw each cell with
an 8x16 font (glyphs from Linux lib/fonts/font_8x16.c, GPL-2.0).
The framebuffer is mapped in machine_init, once kernel VM is up.
multiboot2 parsing now also records the RGB field layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
